SUMMARY:Montclair Story Salon: Tradition! for Family Promise
DESCRIPTION:Montclair Story Salon proudly presents Tradition!\, an evening of storytelling\, music\, and live art on Wednesday\, December 2\, 2026\, at 7:00 PM in the sanctuary at First Congregational Church in Montclair. This special fundraising event will benefit Family Promise of Essex County\, an organization dedicated to helping families experiencing homelessness and housing insecurity find stability\, secure safe housing\, and build brighter futures. The evening will feature stories from:\n• Farnoosh Torabi – Financial journalist\, bestselling author\, and host of the So Money podcast and the beloved Montclair Pod.\n• George Oliphant – Emmy Nominated Host of NBC’s George to the Rescue.\n• Henry H. Neff – bestselling author of the bestselling Tapestry series.\n• Kim Coleman Foote – award-winning author of Coleman Hill.\n• Live music: Ryan Hobler.\n• Live art: Ling Chen\, creating original artwork during the event.\n• Host and MC: Liz Samuel\, founder and producer of Montclair Story Salon.\nMontclair Story Salon is grateful for the generous support of its community sponsors\, including Elaine Pardalos of Brown Harris Stevens NJ Real Estate\, Ironbound Farm Market and Watchung Booksellers\, whose commitment helps make these community-centered events possible.\nJoin us for an unforgettable evening of stories\, music\, art\, and community in support of families in need. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/montclair-story-salon-tradition-for-family-promise/
